# ============================================================
# Smart Home Platform -- Pi Deployment Secrets
# ============================================================
# Copy this file to ".env" on your laptop, fill in the real
# values, and 03-deploy-pi.ps1 will SCP it to the Pi.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# NEVER commit the populated .env. The write-protect hook
# blocks edits to ".env" (exact) and .gitignore excludes it.
# pi-setup.sh sources this file and fails by name if any
# required variable below is missing or empty.
#
# Lines starting with # are comments. Do not wrap values in
# quotes unless the value itself contains spaces.
# ============================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Deployment targets -- used by 03-deploy-pi.ps1 on the LAPTOP
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# These are NOT secrets and are NOT used by the Pi runtime.
# pi-setup.sh ignores them. They tell the deploy orchestrator
# where the PC (source of truth) and the Pi (target) live.
# 01-enable-ssh-on-pc.ps1 prints the correct PC_IP and PC_USER.
# Command-line parameters to 03-deploy-pi.ps1 override these.
PC_IP=
PC_USER=Josh
PI_IP=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Tailscale -- remote access mesh (REQUIRED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# A reusable, pre-authorised auth key so the Pi joins your
# tailnet non-interactively during setup.
# Get it from: https://login.tailscale.com/admin/settings/keys
#   - Click "Generate auth key"
#   - Enable "Reusable" and (for client sites) "Ephemeral: off"
#   - For client devices, attach an ACL tag e.g. tag:client
# Format: tskey-auth-xxxxxxxxxxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
TS_AUTHKEY=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Cloudflare Tunnel -- client-facing remote access (REQUIRED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# The token for a named tunnel. cloudflared runs as a service
# using this token. Creating the tunnel itself is a manual step
# (see setup/pi/PI_SETUP.md "Manual Steps").
# Get it from: https://one.dash.cloudflare.com/
#   - Networks > Tunnels > Create a tunnel > Cloudflared
#   - Copy the token shown in the "install and run" command
# Format: a long opaque eyJ... string
CF_TUNNEL_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Home Assistant connection -- used by ha-core (REQUIRED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# HASS_URL: where ha-core reaches Home Assistant. On the Pi,
# HA runs in a host-network container on the same box, so this
# is the loopback address. Do NOT use the laptop's IP here.
HASS_URL=http://localhost:8123

# HASS_TOKEN: a Home Assistant Long-Lived Access Token.
# Get it from: HA web UI > your profile (bottom left) >
#   Security > Long-lived access tokens > Create token.
# Shown only once -- copy it immediately.
HASS_TOKEN=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Backblaze B2 -- nightly off-site backup (REQUIRED)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# ha-core uploads HA snapshots + SQLite + config to B2 via the
# S3-compatible API. Backups skip gracefully if these are blank.
# Get them from: https://www.backblaze.com/
#   - Account > Application Keys > Add a New Application Key
#   - Scope the key to this site's bucket only
B2_KEY_ID=
B2_APP_KEY=
# The bucket name for this site's config backups.
# Convention: smarthome-<siteid>-config
B2_BUCKET=

# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Future: ops-agent layer (HOME PI ONLY -- leave commented)
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Claude API key for the future ops-agent (log summaries,
# client-hub heartbeat, Frigate event triage). It is NOT used
# by this build. The ops-agent unit ships disabled and must
# never be enabled on a client device. See ops-agent.service.example.
# Get it from: https://console.anthropic.com/ > API Keys
# CLAUDE_OPS_API_KEY=
